#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1002 expect=noViolation domain=DM
#note "FRESH, DISCRIMINATING. ONE row: the start is a June partial and the end is 30 June, so SOME candidate start days are after the end and some are not - lower('2020-06') = 2020-06-01 is NOT greater than upper('2020-06-30') = 2020-06-30, and the universal test therefore answers FALSE. Predicted SILENT. This is the exact companion of invalid_partial_start and the pair is what makes the forall semantics visible: an AMBIGUOUS partial does not fire, a DEFINITE one does. A fire means the comparison became existential rather than universal; escalate, do not rewrite."
